{"id": "EUVD-2026-102482", "enisaUuid": "c6013a31-52a6-31b1-9bbb-fc7422b14855", "description": "rustdesk-api through 2.7 contains an authorization bypass vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to overwrite existing peer records by supplying only a target device ID to POST /api/sysinfo. Attackers can overwrite hostname, username, OS and uuid without uuid verification, then log in presenting that uuid to rebind the peer to their account.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T21:43:32", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T01:43:07", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@hieuPenguinnn/rustdesk-api-sysinfo-unauth-peer-tamper", "https://github.com/lejianwen/rustdesk-api/blob/v2.7/http/router/api.go#L60-L76", "https://github.com/lejianwen/rustdesk-api/blob/v2.7/http/controller/api/peer.go#L26-L57", "https://github.com/lejianwen/rustdesk-api", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/rustdesk-api-through-2.7-authorization-bypass-via-post-api-sysinfo"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111324", "GHSA-qvc9-rg5c-3453"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.32, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "f53f7dbf-47c1-3b88-9330-31ee5bcbc7c9", "product": {"name": "rustdesk-api", "vendor": {"name": "lejianwen"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.7"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1a015d1f-e894-3c2f-afe1-873f7b185e03", "vendor": {"name": "lejianwen"}}], "isExploited": false}